at other food that you  do  so this my friend is a tenderloin of  beef and we're actually using the head  because it's actually separated here  into  two different parts right but for dips  it doesn't matter we're not going to  cook it whole it actually helps us  in ethiopia eating meat is a luxury it's  something that you eat on big holidays  whether it's weddings or spiritual  holidays very often when you have a big  party  you give away a goat you have to call  your goat pimp have that in your phone  i'm not joking the tips that you see  late night is very often in ethiopia  right around bars that's where the cab  drivers are that's where the good eats  are that's where i go  so i'm cutting into cubes like this very  simple pieces and there's really no bad  parts of this but it's super lean you  can do this with flank steak as well  much more affordable but why not black  history month let's celebrate now it's  time to sear it i'm just going to pour a  little oil in and again i have a little  bit sort of leftover pieces we're not  going to throw them out the fat the good  flavor is going to come from that right  we're just going to put that in and  season our pan right so we're using  everything you know we'll be happy your  grandmother the pan is hot  salt  a little bit of pepper  and this guy this is the barbra berbera  is used is our salt and pepper it's used  in everything berber is an ethiopian  spice blend chili pepper  cardamon  sauce dried garlic dried ginger it's all  in there and it's really the thing that  when you've had ethiopian food  this is what you're gonna remember this  is actually even a currency in ethiopia  so i'm putting a good amount on it on  top  i'm keeping this on a high eight and i'm  just gonna coat my meat oh the smells in  the aromas are absolutely  amazing right i smell home when i've  been away on a trip  and i open my door and i miss something  it's very often  the smell of berbere and now do not  clean up the pan we're going to use the  same pan because all the juices and  flavors are in here  i'm going to add in  my broccoli rub and this could be  kale mustard green bottom of the pan has  all the flavorings right it has the meat  it has the meat drippings it has the  berber we're just going to cook it  pretty quick  now we're actually going to start  building up this dish and we're going to  put a little bit of oil  and the  yellow  it's delicious so this adds flavor  i'm going to start with  onion  nice beautiful red onion sliced garlic  and ginger  the flavor's just gonna build here  so this combination between onion and  ginger garlic is also in so much of  ethiopian cooking but it's just going to  caramelize it gets nice i'm going to add  in rosemary  time to add in a little bit of cumin  i love making ethiopian especially  ethiopian american food because my food  then i'm very often taking ethiopian  stew  and you know adding in like pasta into  that or doing a stir fry there like this  and maybe put an egg on it and put it on  the toast i start very often with  ethiopian ingredients  but  end up somewhere else you see all this  good stuff it's caramelizing the onion  the chilies as we're doing that we're  just going to start add in some sort of  the the wetter stuff so this is going to  be a crushed tomatoes vinegar  mustard  berry goes in everything it really is a  way of life the greens that we cooked  off all of that's just gonna simmer  together now the key here is to  rebuilding this right the onions the  garlic needs to cook off the rosemary  all of that is cooking together  simmering together i'm going to add in  the beef now so now we got to work  pretty quick so the meat is in i'm going  to fold in there the  nice  chopped tomato  the last ingredient i'm gonna put in  is a little bit of chopped cilantro and  now it's just giving it a quick stir the  whole process of making tips is around  20 minutes right and we're making food  here now for six to eight people it's a  lot 